# BUGS

No function sets `errno` or raises a floating-point exception, and `math_errhandling` is not defined.
The header declares no `pow`, `tan`, `asin`, `acos`, `atan`, `atan2`, the hyperbolic functions, `cbrt`, `hypot`, `expm1`, `log1p`, `fmin`, `fmax`, `lround`, `lrint`, `nan`, `ilogb` or `logb`, no `long double` functions, and no `M_PI_2` and the other constants but `M_PI` and `M_E`.
